# clause-codegen — Design

Target-agnostic codegen. Consumes a scheduled IR from
clause-schedule. Emits an intermediate representation consumed by
extension targets. Defines the `CodegenTarget` extension-point
contract; the full contract shape is R3 scope.

## Scope

- `Codegen` — top-level codegen driver.
- `TargetIr` — target-agnostic IR consumed by extension codegens.
- `CodegenTarget` trait — extension point. Concrete signature +
  contract finalised in R3.
- `TargetRegistry` — registered codegen targets (built-in + plugin).
  Final shape post-R3.
- `CodegenArtifact` — per-file output bundle.
- Codegen diagnostics.

## Non-scope

- Concrete targets (clause-jomini for Clausewitz, future
  clause-w3, clause-lua). Each ships as its own repo / crate
  implementing CodegenTarget.
- Pass DAG scheduling (clause-schedule).

## Extension-point contract (R3, finalised 2026-04-26)

`CodegenTarget` is a trait that game-specific target repos
(`clause-jomini`, future `clause-w3`, etc.) implement.

```rust
pub trait CodegenTarget: Send + Sync + 'static {
    const NAME: &'static str;
    const VERSION: u32;

    fn accepts(&self, kind: AstNodeKind) -> bool;
    fn stages(&self) -> &'static [Stage];

    fn compile(
        &self,
        unit: &TypedUnit,
        ctx: &mut CodegenCtx<'_>,
    ) -> Result<CodegenOutput, Diagnostic>;

    fn render_diagnostic(&self, err: &TargetError) -> Diagnostic;
}
```

Stages: PreTypecheck / PostTypecheck / CodegenPre / Codegen /
Link. Targets opt in via `stages()`.

`TargetRegistry` is const-sized `[Option<&'static dyn
CodegenTarget>; MAX_TARGETS]`. The `dyn CodegenTarget` is the ONE
exception to the no-dyn discipline; acceptable because (a) it's
static-lifetime, (b) const-sized, (c) limited to the registry
iteration surface while individual `compile` calls monomorphise
via impl bound elsewhere.

Target selection priority: CLI `--target <name>` wins; then
package-level `[targets]` in Clause.toml; then `[workspace.targets]`;
then the built-in fallback (`clause-builtin` — identity codegen
emitting typed IR).

`CodegenCtx<'a>` bundles `&mut DiagnosticSink`, `&mut ArtefactCache`,
and `&Workspace`.

`CodegenOutput` is `{ bytes: Vec<u8>, manifest: ManifestFragment,
references: &'static [SymbolRef] }` — opaque payload +
distribution hints + cross-target reference symbols.

Built-in targets: `clause-builtin` identity codegen only.
Clausewitz / W3 / Lua targets ship in sibling repos.

## Dependencies

- `clause-ir`, `clause-schedule`.
- `#![no_std]`, no alloc.

## Provisional module layout

- `codegen.rs` — top-level Codegen driver.
- `target_ir.rs` — TargetIr types.
- `target.rs` — CodegenTarget trait (R3 contract).
- `registry.rs` — TargetRegistry const-sized `[Option<&'static dyn
  CodegenTarget>; MAX_TARGETS]` + `register` / `get` / `iter`.
- `ctx.rs` — CodegenCtx bundling DiagnosticSink + ArtefactCache +
  Workspace refs.
- `output.rs` — CodegenOutput + ManifestFragment + SymbolRef.
- `selection.rs` — target-selection priority (CLI → package →
  workspace → builtin).
- `builtin.rs` — identity CodegenTarget impl (`clause-builtin`).
- `stage.rs` — Stage enum (PreTypecheck / PostTypecheck /
  CodegenPre / Codegen / Link).
- `artifact.rs` — CodegenArtifact.
- `diagnostics.rs` — codegen error construction.

